{{!-- Excel-only template (ETP-4901) — flat, calculation-friendly export, same
      convention as report-general-ledger's template-excel.hbs: unlike
      template.hbs (HTML preview, which hides whichever of Producto/Almacén/
      Categoría matches the CURRENT "Agrupar por" choice — that's purely an
      HTML-preview space-saving trick, and its dark group-header band has no
      Excel equivalent), this is a plain one-row-per-(product,warehouse) dump
      with ALL THREE dimension columns always present, so the sheet can be
      pivoted directly in Excel regardless of which grouping was selected on
      screen.
      Amount cells use data-cell-type="number" with round2 (this report's
      helpers.js) — never formatCurrency: html-to-xlsx does
      `parseFloat(cell.innerText)` for that type, so a formatted amount would
      silently truncate at the thousands separator. round2 stays a plain
      Number (max 2 decimals, no forced trailing zeros/grouping) purely to
      strip the extra decimal noise m_costing.cost (the Average Costing
      algorithm's running weighted-average) can carry — it does not
      reformat the value like formatCurrency would. --}}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html><head><meta charset="UTF-8">
<style>
  table { border-collapse: collapse; font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; }
  th { font-weight: bold; text-align: left; background: #f1f5f9; }
  th, td { padding: 1px 4px; white-space: nowrap; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
  <table>
    <thead><tr>
      <th>{{meta.labels.productSearchKey}}</th>
      <th>{{meta.labels.product}}</th>
      <th>{{meta.labels.warehouse}}</th>
      <th>{{meta.labels.category}}</th>
      <th>{{meta.labels.uom}}</th>
      <th>{{meta.labels.qtyOnHand}}</th>
      <th>{{meta.labels.unitCost}}</th>
      <th>{{meta.labels.totalValuation}}</th>
    </tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {{#each rows}}
      <tr>
        <td>{{lookup this 'productSearchKey'}}</td>
        <td>{{lookup this 'product'}}</td>
        <td>{{lookup this 'warehouse'}}</td>
        <td>{{lookup this 'category'}}</td>
        <td>{{lookup this 'uom'}}</td>
        <td data-cell-type="number">{{round2 (lookup this 'qtyOnHand')}}</td>
        <td data-cell-type="number">{{round2 (lookup this 'unitCost')}}</td>
        <td data-cell-type="number">{{round2 (lookup this 'totalValuation')}}</td>
      </tr>
      {{/each}}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</body></html>
